{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If</b> — שויתי: like נשתוה, or שמתי, like שויתי ה'." "<b>And quieted</b> — ודוממתי: from the root of דומם, or from דמיון." "<b>And the sense of כגמול</b> — because he mentioned ולא הלכתי, and the gamul has no strength to walk unless it leans on its mother, for immediately it falls. And כגמול עלי נפשי — the sense is doubled." "<b>And the word עלי</b> — like בעיני. And some say: it is a mode of prayer, for I did not set my heart to seek secrets and wonders from myself; only, if I have not set my soul like a gamul upon its mother — like a gamul upon me let my soul be, after the manner: תדבק לשוני לחכי אם לא אזכרכי. And David said: behold, all my trust is in HaShem, and so let Israel do."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 131, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:34.232966756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}